## Phase 8 — Review  ✅ COMPLETE (manual; 3 defects found and fixed)

- [x] 8.1 Security review of the §4 authorization path. The `/security-review` skill could not run
      (`no merge base` against `origin/HEAD`), so this was done by hand, reading every service each
      tool calls. **Three real defects found and fixed:**
  - [x] **S1 — base enumeration leak (HIGH).** `list_bases` with no `spaceId` resolved to no
        resource, so `validPermissions` never ran, and `BaseService.getAllBaseList` filters by
        USER but **not by TOKEN** (unlike `SpaceService.getSpaceList`, which applies
        `filterSpaceListWithAccessToken` at `space.service.ts:117`). A token restricted to one base
        would therefore enumerate every base its owner could see. Fixed by filtering on the token's
        `spaceIds`/`baseIds` in the tool, mirroring `permission.service.ts:243-245`. Three
        regression tests added.
  - [x] **S2 — validation bypass (MEDIUM).** `create_table` and `create_field` skipped the zod
        schemas the REST controllers apply (`tableRoSchema` at
        `table-open-api.controller.ts:154`, `createFieldRoSchema` at
        `field-open-api.controller.ts:124`), making MCP the laxer door into the same services.
        Both now parse with the same schemas.
  - [x] **S3 — error detail leak (LOW).** `toSafeMessage` returned any `Error.message`, so a Prisma
        error would have exposed query fragments and table names to the model. Now only
        `HttpException` messages (deliberately user-facing, i18n-keyed) pass through; everything
        else returns a generic line and the real error goes to the log. Regression test added.
- [x] 8.2 Code review. Also corrected a comment in `discovery.tools.ts` that became inaccurate
      after the S1 fix — it claimed both list tools relied on service-side token filtering, which
      was only ever true of `list_spaces`.
- [x] 8.3 Risk table audited. Every §12 mitigation shipped; the trash-retention risk was
      downgraded by task 1.3 (no pruning is implemented at all).
- [x] 8.4 Verified: no tool reaches any dependency outside the injected context, and `invoke()`
      is the only path to `execute()`. Checked mechanically as well as by reading.
- [x] 8.5 Largest source file is 180 lines (`tool-registry.ts`); largest overall is the 386-line
      unit spec. All well under 500.
- [x] 8.6 Change is additive. Modified outside the new files: `app.module.ts` (+3),
      `config.module.ts` (+2), `package.json` (+1), `.eslintrc.js` (+10, scoped override for the
      MCP SDK's subpath exports), `openapi/src/index.ts` (+1), and the i18n registration.
- [x] **GATE I — cleared.** S1, S2 and S3 fixed with regression tests; the create-without-delete
      asymmetry is consciously accepted and recorded in design §5.

