## Sequencing notes

- Gates A, B, H and I are the real ones. C–G are progress checkpoints; **H and I are refusals** —
  do not ship past them.
- **Task 1.3 (trash retention) is design-affecting.** If retention is short, design §6.1's premise
  weakens and §6.2 needs a stronger guard. Do it before any code.
- Phases 3→4→5 are ordered by blast radius. Each proves the authorization pipeline against a wider
  surface before the next widens it further.
- Phase 6 can start once Phase 3 lands (the manifest only needs the registry), but the page is not
  demoable until Phase 5 fills the catalogue.
- Phase 7 is written as a phase for clarity; in practice tests land **with** each phase. Nothing
  reaches Phase 8 with untested tools.
- D5 shrank the surface substantially. If the work feels larger than the catalogue justifies,
  something has drifted — re-read §5 before adding anything.

